WEBVTT

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.650
Konomama zutto yukunone.
<i>I bet we're gonna keep going like this.</i>

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.680
Uso wo tsumikasanetemo.
<i>Even if one lie leads to another.</i>

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.620
Kono michi wo nidoto...
<i>We'll never be able...</i>

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.630
...modoru koto wa dekinai
<i>... to go back on this path again.</i>

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.630
Ano toki fumihazushita...
<i>On the other side of the borderline</i>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.660
...kyoukaisen no mukou ni.
<i>... you crossed that time.</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.600
Kimi wa donna yume egaite...
<i>What kind of dreams did you paint...</i>

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.300
...ochite itta?
<i>... as you fell?</i>

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.870
Ashita niwa mietekuru...
<i>The future that becomes visible tomorrow...</i>

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.070
...mirai nante roku demo nai kedo
<i>... isn't really that great,</i>

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.710
Moshikashitara sonnamono ni...
<i>Butjust maybe we're living...</i>

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.340
...sugaritsuite ikiteiru
<i>... clinging on to it anyway.</i>

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.050
Kitto hontou wa kimi mo watashi mo...
<i>I bet you and I are looking for...</i>

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.020
...chigau basho de onaji mono wo
<i>... the same thing in different places.</i>

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.150
Sagashiteru, kanjiteru...
<i>Searching and feeling...</i>

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.860
...tatta hitotsu no shinjitsu.
<i>... for the one, single truth.</i>

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.730
Soredake wo tada shiritakute...
<i>I want to know it so badly...</i>

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.830
...nanimo motazuni koko ni iru.
<i>... that I am here holding nothing.</i>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.630
Yume to utsutsu wo samayou...
<i>Drifting between dream and reality...</i>

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.900
We're too close to the edge!

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.610
Konomama zutto yukunone.
<i>I bet we're gonna keep going like this.</i>

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.640
Uso wo tsumikasanetemo.
<i>Even if one lie leads to another.</i>

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.150
Fumihazushita michi wo...
<i>We'll never be able to return...</i>

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.620
...modoru koto wa dekinai.
<i>... to the path you stepped out of again.</i>

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.550
Kimi ga ima doko ni ite...
<i>No matter where you are now...</i>

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.460
...nani wo mitsumete itemo,
<i>... or what you are looking at,</i>

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:28.620
Sonna fuuni kokorohanashita mama...
<i>Even when our hearts are apart like that...</i>

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.360
...futari wa aishiauno!
<i>... we will still love each other!</i>

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.720
I'll let you off easy this time.
Forget your silly fantasy.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.420
It's not a fantasy, and you know it...

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.990
You're just trying to silence me
because you're in on it...

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.230
Don't forget that you're the ones
who got me fired up about this.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:15.500
If you wanna battle it out, you'd better
find some proof that you can use in court.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.710
Ow!

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.440
It's not the end yet...

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.350
I won't let it end.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.940
How bad is it?!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:19.960
How's the other one doing?!

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.000
He's stabilizing!

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.660
Dad, are they okay?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.530
Did you call us?

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.440
I found them passed out
in the clubhouse.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:51.630
Clubhouse?

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:55.940
G-Study, it's a game research society.
They didn't respond to my voice.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.970
So they haven't vomited?

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.410
No... They're okay, right?

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.440
Doctor!!

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.160
Ah...

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.430
Mai!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.450
At any rate, take them
to the emergency room.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.220
Mai!

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:54.630
I went to your house,
but no one was there.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:56.640
Y- Yeah.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.540
Are you still under the weather?

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:02.670
No, not at all.
I'm just ditching class.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.700
That's no good.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.720
C'mon, you should come to school already.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.890
I know there are a lot of
rumors going around, but...

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.190
Rumors?

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.590
Well... you know. Lots of things.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.670
Everyone's worried about you.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.460
- They aren't mad?
- About what?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.000
Everyone, like Uchiyama...
everyone in G-Study.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.130
The room's sealed off, right?

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:39.200
Yeah, but there was no choice.
Tomonari's condition hasn't changed.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.880
So, he hasn't woken up yet.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.590
Dad also says he can't
make any sense of it.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:54.990
He says that usually, a heater or furnace
is on when something like that happens.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:57.620
But it wasn't anything
like that, right?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:01.230
Besides, you regained
consciousness soon after.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.090
But he didn't.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.230
Uh, no... That's not what I meant.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.410
I'll start going to school again tomorrow.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:18.380
Great. Here's your satchel and violin...
You can't leave them lying around forever.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.390
But, hey, aren't you cold? You should
dress more warmly by the river.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.890
It's the sound...

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.590
If I go there, I don't
have to listen to the sound.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.080
It's all right,
c'mon, have a seat.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.110
But I...

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.610
Here.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.720
Violin practice?

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:35.420
Okay, half an hour...
Just 10 minutes will be fine.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.390
You don't play games, do you?

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.800
Try it! You'll love it!

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.240
It looks kind of difficult...

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:51.140
It's okay. I've put
together your character.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.740
What do you mean?

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:57.270
Just watch...
I'm pretty good at this.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.150
Although I'm not as good as
"The Descendent of Fianna."

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.600
Hello, this is the Minase residence.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.840
Oh, Dad...

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.020
Y- Yeah... Huh?

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.520
She's not home yet.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.290
<i>I see. Actually, about next month...</i>

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.990
You can't come home?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.430
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.630
It's okay. Don't push yourself.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.260
<i>I'm sorry. I'll definitely be home for
the first anniversary of grandpa's death.</i>

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.300
<i>Please tell that to your mother...</i>

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:56.040
<i>Now, are you still not going
to school? Are you still sick?</i>

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.550
<i>Mai? Can you hear me? Hello?</i>

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:08.490
<i>Hello?!</i>

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.160
- Morning!
- Yo!

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.670
Say, say, did you see?!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.690
- Huh?
- Hurry, c'mon!

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.690
Are you the one who
passed out at school?

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:57.770
You are, aren't you? Say, the kid
who was carried out with you...

00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.970
Is he your boyfriend?

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:02.740
Why do I have to tell you that?

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.740
When it happened,
were you playing a game?

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:10.170
I don't know!

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:26.060
Hey, hey!

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:42.450
Mai! I heard you went through
a lot! Are you okay now?

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:43.450
Yeah.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.210
That's good...

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.550
But Tomonari is still
in the hospital, right?

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:49.890
I think so.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.820
You THINK so?

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.820
Mai, he's your boyfriend, isn't he?

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.420
Uh-huh...

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.920
You're awfully calm. That's amazing.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.270
What? Oh, no! Did I upset you?

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.770
I didn't mean to.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:09.610
I need to use the bathroom.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:36.630
You don't have to act so startled...
You'll hurt my feelings.

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:40.200
Hold on.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:49.820
Don't you want to know
why you passed out?

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.320
The reason I passed out?

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:56.050
The World...
You know it, don't you?

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.080
Mai!!

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.960
Who is this guy?

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.990
An acquaintance.

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:06.220
C'mon, don't mess with me!

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.340
I'm Junichiro Tokuoka, 34 years old...

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.670
...currently unemployed,
no address due to circumstances.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:15.570
Do you want to know my hobbies
and body measurements, too?

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:18.770
Only club members are allowed here.
Please leave!

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:23.150
What are you?
A knight protecting the princess?

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:28.920
All right! I'm leaving...

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.590
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:38.960
It's not good to play games
all the time, kids!

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.800
Mai, see you later!

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:48.010
Voluptuous

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.510
He said "The World"?

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:50.010
Her

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.040
Yes.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.950
Did something happen in the game?

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:55.480
Remnant
I wouldn't put it past Tomonari
to try something reckless...

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:58.350
I wouldn't put it past Tomonari
to try something reckless...

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:00.150
Do you remember where you went?

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.620
What do you mean, where?

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.650
Like the area Keywords.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.780
I dunno.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.920
Then what do you remember?

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:12.190
I think we were in
a town square-like place...

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:15.130
That's the Root Town. Then what?

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.600
That's all I remember.

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:18.900
Hmm...

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.840
I can't help it...
It was my first time playing a game.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.040
Did something happen
between you and Tomonari?

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.070
No, nothing.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.980
What if something had happened?

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.580
Uh, nothing...

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:01.980
An Interview With Junichiro Tokuoka

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.820
What's her problem?

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.130
Mai!

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.110
Where have you been recently?

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:36.050
Um, busy...

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:39.310
Did you hear that they announced
the set piece we're going to perform?

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.120
No, not yet...

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.780
It's going to be
pretty tough this time.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.190
Um, I gotta go. I'm sorry.

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:50.130
She might be a lost cause.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.290
Hey, Kie...

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:55.830
What's wrong with that?
It means one less rival. Right?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.710
He's with CC Corporation? Him?

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.610
What does that mean?

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.740
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.220
- Mai...
- <i>Hmm?</i>

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.990
You can always choose to do nothing.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.790
You can leave that man to his own business.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:26.660
Besides that... Dad wants you to come in
one more time for an examination, just in case.

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.760
- <i>And I...</i>
- Huh?

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.130
<i>I want to stop worrying, too.</i>

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:36.170
<i>Huh? Did I say something funny?</i>

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.310
See ya!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.740
Oh, hey, sis!

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:48.850
Big brother... is it true that
Mai might stop playing the violin?

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.080
Who told you that?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:56.690
A senior in my class. If she stopped
coming, that class would suck.

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.200
Hi!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.500
What?

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:13.210
That guy, Tokuoka isn't part of CC Corp.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.080
What?

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:18.210
They told me he quit half a year ago.
I harassed them at the customer center.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.280
After I got transferred a million times...

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:23.450
...they finally said
"He has nothing to do with our company."

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:30.690
I thought that the sooner
you knew, the better, that's all.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.760
Well, see you at school...

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:37.900
Say, I know this is
none of my business...

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:39.930
...but don't quit the violin.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:45.410
Even if you stop going to
music class, keep playing it.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.110
Okay?

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.050
Okay.

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.680
Nothing out of the ordinary!

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:00.490
Aren't you happy?

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:03.760
Doctor... Can subliminal information...

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:08.170
...cause someone to lose consciousness?

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.730
Nope.

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.900
There's no possibility?

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:16.070
Subliminal suggestion itself
is like an urban myth.

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:19.240
It never produces results
like the ones you hear about.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.080
It's been medically proven.

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:25.410
Don't tell me! You think
it was the game that did it?

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:35.960
I recall that you claimed you began
to feel sick as you were playing a game...

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:40.190
...and the next thing you knew,
you had been brought here.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:42.100
I'm not making it up.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.340
Yes... However, Mai...

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:52.270
I heard from Masaya...

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:58.310
"The World," hm? They say that over
20 million copies have been sold worldwide.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.350
Use your common sense. Just think.

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:10.420
It just isn't possible.

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:27.080
<i>Why? I don't understand...
Why didn't he wake up, too?</i>

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.180
H- Hey!

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.090
Wait! Wait!

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.360
I'll let go!
I'll let go of you, see?

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:47.460
Please don't do anything.
I'm begging you.

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:48.930
Mm-hm.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.960
- Really?
- Mm-hm.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.660
Okay, you promised...

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.300
What are you doing here?!

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.100
I wanted to see his face.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:03.010
I had to see this boy...

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.140
If you don't stop lying,
I'll call someone.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:10.310
Why don't you believe me?

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:14.160
There would be a panic if it became known
that someone passed out because of the game.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:17.020
Is that why you're
going around threatening people?

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:21.260
Mai, you got it all wrong.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:25.340
I'm not with CC Corp.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.000
I know that!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:29.480
You quit so you'd have nothing
to do with the company...

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:31.770
...so you can freely do
your dirty work! Didn't you?!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.570
That's some good detective work...
However...

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:40.280
No, you're wrong!
Where you're mistaken...

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.850
...is probably the fact
that I'm on your side.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.760
I think I will call someone!

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.450
No, don't!
C'mon, Mai. Be reasonable!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.020
Hey!

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:03.270
I wonder if he's still
in the game right now...

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.540
...still fighting some battle?

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:13.580
Won't you help me out?

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:01.660
What's his name?
What name did he play under?

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.190
Sieg. S. I. E. G.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:08.500
What's his password?

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:10.530
Mai Minase.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.400
I see... I should've figured.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:26.030
- Uh-oh!
- What?!

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:28.550
I accidentally opened up
the mail out of habit.

00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:36.030
Yukichin and Kyo.

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.170
Do you know them?

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:40.540
Do you remember
which server you went to?

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:44.910
You said it was your first time
playing a game, didn't you?

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:50.580
Then it would probably be Delta.
I guess I'll find out if I check the log.

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:05.090
Take this!

00:22:09.570 --> 00:22:11.560
Not again...

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:20.100
Why are you so quiet?
What do you mean by "again"?

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.810
How long have you been doing this?

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:30.750
Listen...

00:22:32.230 --> 00:22:36.750
There are at least six people in
Tomonari's same condition in Japan.

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:43.660
Of those who went into a coma...
no one has recovered.

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:45.470
Listen, no one.

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:15.930
What happened in the game?

00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:18.440
How did you come back safely?

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:21.170
I don't remember. I don't know!

00:23:39.790 --> 00:23:41.760
Who's there?

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:47.260
A sound? Where?

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:18.960
A in C major?

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:22.590
The "Ah" sound... It's used
for tuning musical instruments.

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:24.160
That's what it was...

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:24.760
Huh?

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:28.740
Uh, no... So, you're saying you heard
that before losing consciousness?

00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:30.440
Yeah.

00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:34.480
Hmm... But I wonder?

00:24:34.520 --> 00:24:37.640
That sound has been
bothering me ever since...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:39.650
...but I'm having trouble remembering.

00:24:39.690 --> 00:24:43.210
Although I'm sure it's what
I heard in the game.

00:24:43.260 --> 00:24:48.460
Mai, when you came to at the hospital,
the first thing you said was "Ah... - ."

00:24:48.500 --> 00:24:49.620
I did?!

00:24:49.660 --> 00:24:53.620
That was "Ahhh" as in
A, B, C in German, wasn't it?

00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:57.570
That's why I think you
definitely heard that sound.

00:24:57.600 --> 00:24:59.600
Maybe you couldn't
remember it until now...

00:24:59.640 --> 00:25:03.840
...because you shielded yourself
subconsciously from it somehow.

00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:05.610
But still...

00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:11.180
But the sound has nothing
to do with me passing out?!

00:25:14.690 --> 00:25:19.150
At least, it's probably not good
to jump to conclusions. Besides...

00:25:19.960 --> 00:25:22.220
Your sense of hearing is
out of the ordinary, right?

00:25:22.260 --> 00:25:24.790
Can you say for sure that it
was a sound inside the game?

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:28.190
I...

00:25:28.770 --> 00:25:31.200
You shouldn't dwell on it too much.

00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:37.940
Do you know the meaning
of his character name?

00:25:37.980 --> 00:25:39.310
Do you mean Sieg?

00:25:39.350 --> 00:25:44.110
There's this extremely strong guy in the game,
I don't know who he is or where he is from...

00:25:44.150 --> 00:25:47.280
...but he calls himself
"Balmung of the Azure Sky."

00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:50.550
By Balmung, do you mean
Siegfried's sword?

00:25:50.590 --> 00:25:51.790
You know a lot!

00:25:51.830 --> 00:25:56.730
Grandpa loved the Ring...
"Der Ring des Nibelungen."

00:25:58.330 --> 00:26:00.320
Wagner?

00:26:01.740 --> 00:26:03.700
So, it's Siegfried.

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:07.670
Yeah. He said he would become
the possessor, and not the sword.

00:26:09.040 --> 00:26:12.840
Tomonari is amazing in the game.
He rapidly got more powerful...

00:26:14.280 --> 00:26:17.680
Say, Siegfried is invincible, right?

00:26:19.990 --> 00:26:23.650
lfTomonari doesn't wake up...

00:26:23.690 --> 00:26:26.990
If he stays like this forever, just aging...

00:26:27.030 --> 00:26:28.790
Mai...

00:26:28.830 --> 00:26:32.460
I promise I won't let
Tomonari stay this way.

00:26:33.770 --> 00:26:37.200
After all, I'm the one who
invited him to try "The World..."

00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:48.370
Hello, this is the Minase residence.

00:26:48.950 --> 00:26:50.940
Huh? Uh...

00:26:52.750 --> 00:26:53.910
...hello.

00:26:54.790 --> 00:26:57.220
Ah, there you are!

00:26:57.260 --> 00:27:00.720
I wanted to apologize about yesterday.

00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:03.200
I wasn't acting mature.

00:27:03.230 --> 00:27:05.560
I'm sorry. Will you forgive me?

00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:11.700
You will? Really?
Okay, now that's settled...

00:27:12.670 --> 00:27:14.660
Wait, don't hang up yet!

00:27:15.410 --> 00:27:19.900
Yeah. Now that we're friends again,
I have another favor to ask.

00:27:21.520 --> 00:27:23.570
<i>Can I go into the clubhouse?</i>

00:27:24.520 --> 00:27:25.880
The G-Study room?

00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:28.910
<i>Yeah... The place
where you two passed out.</i>

00:27:30.820 --> 00:27:35.320
<i>I want to test it one more time in the same
environment under the same circumstances.</i>

00:27:35.360 --> 00:27:36.420
What?

00:27:38.600 --> 00:27:43.930
Maybe we're the only ones who think
that the game is the cause of the coma.

00:27:45.510 --> 00:27:47.940
<i>C'mon, work with me.</i>

00:27:50.180 --> 00:27:52.170
I need a little time.

00:27:53.950 --> 00:27:54.440
Hideous
Organ Market
Scaffold

00:27:58.520 --> 00:27:59.850
I...

00:27:59.890 --> 00:28:02.880
There must be something wrong
with me... I'm an idiot.

00:28:04.990 --> 00:28:06.820
I won't do it again...

00:28:06.860 --> 00:28:09.690
...for a while. I mean...
I'm sorry!

00:28:10.900 --> 00:28:12.730
It doesn't really bother me...

00:28:12.770 --> 00:28:14.860
You're not upset?

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:15.870
Cool!

00:28:15.900 --> 00:28:17.460
I have to go now.

00:28:18.140 --> 00:28:20.200
Ugh, look at this mess...

00:28:22.010 --> 00:28:24.340
Anyways, have a seat, have a seat.

00:28:24.380 --> 00:28:26.240
But I...

00:28:26.280 --> 00:28:27.680
C'mon!

00:28:39.860 --> 00:28:43.420
You've got to be kidding!
Are you still in contact with that man?!

00:28:46.170 --> 00:28:47.360
Well...

00:28:47.400 --> 00:28:49.870
Should you be trusting him?

00:28:49.900 --> 00:28:52.870
I don't know...

00:28:52.910 --> 00:28:55.340
Mai... What's wrong with you?

00:28:56.180 --> 00:28:59.270
I don't know why,
but I want to know!

00:29:00.880 --> 00:29:04.250
I want to know what
happened in the game.

00:29:05.950 --> 00:29:09.320
I have to know.
But to do that...

00:29:09.360 --> 00:29:11.980
You have to sneak into the clubhouse
in the middle of the night...

00:29:12.030 --> 00:29:14.020
...with a shady middle-aged man?

00:29:14.930 --> 00:29:16.520
You don't have to put it that way...

00:29:16.560 --> 00:29:18.690
C'mon... Think about it calmly.

00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:21.100
After all, it's just a game.

00:29:21.130 --> 00:29:25.870
It's impossible for someone to
go into a coma over a silly game.

00:29:27.270 --> 00:29:32.610
I don't know what that Tokuoka guy
was thinking when he said that to you.

00:29:32.650 --> 00:29:35.010
But I can say this for certain...

00:29:35.050 --> 00:29:37.780
He's definitely up to something!
It's too suspicious!

00:29:43.420 --> 00:29:45.690
I think I made a mistake.

00:29:46.130 --> 00:29:47.990
Yeah.

00:29:48.430 --> 00:29:50.690
I was relying on you too heavily.

00:29:52.430 --> 00:29:54.200
H... Hey, Mai!

00:29:55.470 --> 00:29:57.490
Just forget what we were talking about.

00:29:57.540 --> 00:29:59.200
Wait!

00:30:00.010 --> 00:30:02.000
I'm sorry.

00:30:19.190 --> 00:30:21.020
You're home early today.

00:30:21.060 --> 00:30:26.430
Mai, I took a quick work-break.
I'll need to head back soon...

00:30:26.930 --> 00:30:28.730
Don't just stand there.
Come over here.

00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:41.340
I hear that you haven't been going to
music class. What's the meaning of this?

00:30:41.980 --> 00:30:43.970
I...

00:30:45.050 --> 00:30:47.020
I know that you've had a difficult time.

00:30:47.050 --> 00:30:50.990
That's why I didn't say anything
when you didn't go to school.

00:30:51.020 --> 00:30:53.020
But the violin is different, isn't it?

00:30:56.800 --> 00:30:59.460
Mai, do you think you'll
become a soloist this way?

00:31:00.030 --> 00:31:02.470
I've never thought of becoming a soloist.

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:06.170
There you go again...

00:31:06.210 --> 00:31:07.610
Well, I've never...

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:09.610
We've already had this conversation.

00:31:10.010 --> 00:31:12.440
You said you would become
a soloist, that's why...

00:31:12.480 --> 00:31:15.070
I like the violin, that's all.

00:31:16.020 --> 00:31:18.280
If you just like it as
a hobby, then give it up!

00:31:19.250 --> 00:31:21.220
Why does it have to be like that?

00:31:22.090 --> 00:31:25.750
Your late grandfather was
the only hobbyist I can take.

00:31:25.790 --> 00:31:29.320
If you're going to play it,
you must keep a firm goal in mind.

00:31:29.360 --> 00:31:31.520
Right, Mai?

00:31:31.570 --> 00:31:33.860
What you're saying isn't right, Mom...

00:31:34.870 --> 00:31:38.670
I see... You have your
grandfather's blood in you.

00:31:39.510 --> 00:31:41.500
I understand.

00:31:43.580 --> 00:31:45.340
M- Mom?

00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:51.140
Mai, you don't have to go
to violin class anymore!

00:31:51.180 --> 00:31:52.780
There's no need for
your violin anymore, either!

00:31:53.790 --> 00:31:56.780
Stop it! Mom! Mom!

00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:28.080
Hi!

00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:31.090
Answer one thing for me.

00:32:31.120 --> 00:32:32.220
What is it?

00:32:32.260 --> 00:32:34.730
What is your goal?

00:32:34.760 --> 00:32:39.030
My goal, huh? Let me think...
It's the same as yours.

00:32:39.070 --> 00:32:41.000
I also want to know
what the heck happened...

00:32:41.030 --> 00:32:45.660
...that day, at that time,
in that playing field.

00:32:46.570 --> 00:32:48.560
Why?

00:32:49.180 --> 00:32:51.440
You asked for one answer...

00:32:52.210 --> 00:32:54.150
...and I responded.

00:32:54.180 --> 00:32:56.170
Well, let's go!

00:32:57.350 --> 00:32:59.340
It's pretty secure.

00:33:00.290 --> 00:33:04.720
Oh, I almost forgot... Mai,
you're a fast runner, right?

00:33:31.790 --> 00:33:34.350
Oops. You mean Mai?

00:33:35.220 --> 00:33:37.420
I asked her to go out with me.

00:33:37.460 --> 00:33:39.450
Uh, keep this a secret!

00:33:41.130 --> 00:33:43.290
Didn't you say you didn't like her?

00:33:43.800 --> 00:33:47.530
Actually, I thought
that she didn't like ME.

00:33:47.570 --> 00:33:49.260
That's because you pick on her!

00:33:49.300 --> 00:33:51.900
You mean my childish
expressions of affection?

00:33:53.870 --> 00:33:57.880
Maybe she thought you'd start picking
on her again if she didn't say yes.

00:33:57.880 --> 00:33:58.380
Dog Dancing
Passionate
Tri Pansy

00:33:58.380 --> 00:33:59.480
Huh? For real?!

00:33:59.480 --> 00:34:01.540
I said maybe.

00:34:02.380 --> 00:34:04.820
I hope not! I won't know what to do!

00:34:06.690 --> 00:34:10.780
No, Mai isn't the type
to say yes over something like that.

00:34:12.390 --> 00:34:14.380
Maybe not.

00:34:35.420 --> 00:34:38.410
Oh? It's way past lights out.

00:34:50.060 --> 00:34:52.860
Now, how shall we do this?

00:34:52.900 --> 00:34:54.890
It's this way.

00:34:56.440 --> 00:34:58.100
H- Hey...

00:34:59.410 --> 00:35:01.400
What? Which way?

00:35:14.220 --> 00:35:16.350
You're gonna break that?
For reals?!

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:19.150
I think you should stop
using that expression.

00:35:31.100 --> 00:35:33.200
Where's...

00:35:33.240 --> 00:35:34.430
Got it.

00:35:46.350 --> 00:35:47.880
Oh, my...

00:35:47.920 --> 00:35:50.410
- Is something wrong?
- No, it's nothing.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:57.990
Is this it?

00:36:01.700 --> 00:36:04.930
Because it's a program
you ported yourself?

00:36:06.970 --> 00:36:09.640
Why didn't you go on with
what you were saying earlier?

00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:11.370
Do I have to say it?

00:36:11.410 --> 00:36:14.280
When you ask someone a favor,
you normally explain everything.

00:36:14.980 --> 00:36:16.970
I'm afraid.

00:36:19.690 --> 00:36:24.990
I'm afraid of why this happened
and why nobody realized it...

00:36:25.360 --> 00:36:28.990
...but most of all, I'm afraid of why
I didn't realize it all this time...

00:36:29.660 --> 00:36:31.720
And I'm pissed off at all
the other idiots around me, too!

00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:35.900
Oh, should I stop using
"pissed off," too?

00:36:37.600 --> 00:36:39.400
Are you investigating incognito?

00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:42.930
Incognito? You've got
a heck of a vocabulary.

00:36:42.980 --> 00:36:43.970
What do you mean?

00:36:50.620 --> 00:36:55.280
Oh, well. Anyways, we're going
to see Sieg again in several ways.

00:36:56.520 --> 00:36:58.510
But Sieg isn't...

00:37:06.370 --> 00:37:08.430
Everything has a back door.

00:37:08.870 --> 00:37:11.500
There's one to the clubhouse,
and even one to "The World."

00:37:12.440 --> 00:37:15.170
It's the same in the real world
as it is in the game.

00:37:16.410 --> 00:37:20.610
If someone goes missing,
there are always traces.

00:37:20.650 --> 00:37:24.880
The last place they were seen,
a verified time when they went missing...

00:37:25.890 --> 00:37:30.120
...if you can grasp the outline of a void,
it will eventually become proof of the real image.

00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:36.520
As long as his data is left on
the server, we can do something.

00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:41.390
"Mai Minase."

00:37:41.770 --> 00:37:45.260
Because you told me his
login name and password...

00:37:45.310 --> 00:37:48.070
...it was relatively easy
to locate his data.

00:37:49.080 --> 00:37:51.100
And this...

00:37:56.350 --> 00:37:58.340
You've seen this before, haven't you?

00:37:59.620 --> 00:38:03.420
Sieg 2. It's like a clone.

00:38:03.460 --> 00:38:05.790
The name is different,
but the contents are the same.

00:38:08.060 --> 00:38:11.000
This is the town you came to, right?

00:38:17.970 --> 00:38:22.470
Now, Mai. In order to
recreate the same circumstances...

00:38:22.510 --> 00:38:25.500
...you'll have to access along with me.

00:38:25.810 --> 00:38:27.040
I know.

00:38:27.080 --> 00:38:30.240
Are you sure? You might
lose consciousness again.

00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:34.240
And this time, it's possible
that you won't wake up...

00:38:34.950 --> 00:38:37.150
That should apply to you as well.

00:38:37.590 --> 00:38:40.620
That's true. Maybe we should
give up and just go home.

00:38:41.090 --> 00:38:42.490
You're right.

00:38:42.530 --> 00:38:44.460
You're kidding...

00:38:44.500 --> 00:38:48.870
I am kidding. It's all right.
I won't pass out.

00:38:49.200 --> 00:38:50.760
I have the sound.

00:39:10.660 --> 00:39:12.920
All that's left is to enter the field.

00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:15.120
- Right.
- Well, let's go!

00:39:16.300 --> 00:39:18.730
The Keywords are
Chosen Hopeless Nothingness!

00:39:23.570 --> 00:39:26.200
It looks like a plain-old
run-of-the-mill playing field...

00:39:27.170 --> 00:39:28.160
Something's there!

00:39:28.210 --> 00:39:30.200
Yeah. That's just a minor character.

00:39:31.640 --> 00:39:35.600
The enemy characters are also normal.
Do you remember which way you went?

00:39:36.150 --> 00:39:37.620
No.

00:39:37.650 --> 00:39:39.170
Wanna check out the dungeon?

00:39:39.890 --> 00:39:44.150
If we find out something here,
will Tomonari regain consciousness?

00:39:46.630 --> 00:39:48.620
In all honesty, that's...

00:39:52.270 --> 00:39:53.990
This sound!

00:39:54.030 --> 00:39:57.130
Sound? There's nothing playing
except for the background music.

00:40:00.740 --> 00:40:02.730
It's coming!

00:40:06.550 --> 00:40:07.880
What?

00:40:10.780 --> 00:40:11.910
Run!

00:40:11.950 --> 00:40:13.780
Where is it?

00:40:15.590 --> 00:40:17.890
- It's coming from the left!
- Where?!

00:41:00.270 --> 00:41:02.260
Mr. Tokuoka!

00:41:03.770 --> 00:41:05.740
Mr. Tokuoka!!

00:41:09.040 --> 00:41:11.030
Mr. Tokuoka?!

00:41:14.310 --> 00:41:16.300
Mr. Tokuoka!!

00:41:25.660 --> 00:41:27.650
Mr. Tokuoka!

00:42:02.130 --> 00:42:04.650
Masaya! Help him, quickly!

00:42:05.930 --> 00:42:07.920
How did this happen?!

00:42:16.710 --> 00:42:17.730
Mai?

00:42:17.780 --> 00:42:19.440
It's okay.

00:42:20.150 --> 00:42:22.210
He'll wake up soon.

00:42:22.250 --> 00:42:24.240
What about you?

00:42:28.720 --> 00:42:31.690
"The World" isn't just a game.

00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:34.350
Then what is it?

00:42:34.930 --> 00:42:38.830
I think this man is looking
for the answer to that...

00:42:39.700 --> 00:42:41.460
...and so am I.

00:42:53.410 --> 00:42:55.400
Ouch...

00:42:56.520 --> 00:43:00.710
See, didn't I tell you?
I'm sure that Tomonari will wake up, too.

00:43:03.820 --> 00:43:05.810
Mr. Tokuoka!

00:43:06.790 --> 00:43:08.780
That hurt!

00:43:10.660 --> 00:43:13.000
Are you all right, Mr. Tokuoka?

00:43:13.900 --> 00:43:16.930
Hi, partner. Are you sick of this yet?

00:43:17.440 --> 00:43:18.840
How about you?

00:43:18.870 --> 00:43:20.960
Nope. I'm not done yet.

00:43:24.080 --> 00:43:25.700
It's only the beginning.

00:43:25.750 --> 00:43:27.740
Yeah. It's just the beginning.

00:43:36.820 --> 00:43:41.420
Tasogare no umi ni dete...
<i>Setting out in twilight seas...</i>

00:43:41.460 --> 00:43:46.400
Futari wa nidoto mou meguri...
<i>Will we never meet...</i>

00:43:46.400 --> 00:43:50.890
...aenaino?
<i>... again?</i>

00:43:58.080 --> 00:44:05.480
Kin no akari ga umi ni ochite...
<i>A light of gold falls into the sea...</i>

00:44:05.790 --> 00:44:11.020
...natsu no kaze ga togireta.
<i>... the wind of summer is cut off.</i>

00:44:11.060 --> 00:44:16.360
Obieru futari ni tada...
<i>The frightened pair only hears the sound...</i>

00:44:16.400 --> 00:44:22.360
...yosetekaesu mizuoto.
<i>... of sea water coming and going again.</i>

00:44:24.200 --> 00:44:29.400
Donnani nami wo kasanete...
<i>No matter how I drown the waves...</i>

00:44:29.440 --> 00:44:34.810
Omoide wo sakendemo...
<i>Screaming out our memories...</i>

00:44:34.850 --> 00:44:40.050
Anata no ita kishibe niwa...
<i>I can never return to the shore...</i>

00:44:40.090 --> 00:44:45.620
...mou kaerenai.
<i>... where you were.</i>

00:44:46.190 --> 00:44:50.820
Tasogare dake wo daite.
<i>Embrace nothing but the twilight sky.</i>

00:44:50.860 --> 00:44:53.990
Ano hi no nami wa mou...
<i>The waves from that day are now...</i>

00:44:54.030 --> 00:44:57.830
...fukai umi no soko.
<i>... at the bottom of the deep ocean.</i>

00:44:57.870 --> 00:45:01.470
Kanashimi wo shiranai...
<i>They sleep as they embrace blue dream...</i>

00:45:01.510 --> 00:45:06.810
...aoi yume wo mite nemutteiru.
<i>... that does not know sorrow.</i>
